{
  "key": "auto-assembly",
  "name": "Automotive Assembly Plant",
  "category": "mixed",
  "description": "Discrete/automotive plant (Purdue L1-L4): corporate LAN, IT/OT DMZ, plant operations (MES, historian, TIA + Studio 5000 engineering, IIoT edge gateway) and three cells. BODY-SHOP: a redundant S7-1500R pair (PLC-BIW-R1 primary / R2 backup, sync carried as PROFINET RT between them) driving ET 200SP stations and KUKA KR C4 robots over PROFINET RT, on an MRP ring managed by a SCALANCE XC208; every PN device announces LLDP. PAINT-SHOP: PLCnext AXC F 2152 controllers with Beckhoff EK9300 couplers (PROFINET), WAGO PFC200 oven controllers (Modbus/TCP), Beckhoff CX5140 booth PCs (OPC UA) on a Hirschmann MRP ring. ASSEMBLY: three Rockwell CompactLogix 5380 lines, each a DLR ring supervisor with POINT I/O, 12 identical PowerFlex 525 drives and FANUC R-30iB Plus robots on CIP class-1 I/O. EDGE-GW01 (SIMATIC IOT2050) reads the PLCs over OPC UA and publishes MQTT + Sparkplug B in cleartext to a cloud broker (external CLOUD-MQTT, 18.193.47.120). Planted findings: (1) PROFINET DCP Set-IP from the integrator laptop LAPTOP-INTEG to ET-BIW-05; (2) duplicate NameOfStation 'et-biw-03' on ET-BIW-03 and ET-BIW-07; (3) VNC (RFB) open on KUKA robot ROB-BIW-04 (Windows 7 Embedded, BlueKeep) reached from ENG-TIA across zones; (4) OT edge gateway talking cleartext MQTT to the internet. Periods: PN-RT 32 ms update time, CIP I/O 100 ms (Forward_Open states a 20 ms RPI), MRP test frames 50 ms (500 ms recovery profile), DLR beacons 100 ms (the frames state the 400 µs default; slowed so a capture stays readable).",
